[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5419391545","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5419391545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5419391545,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQwVaOQ","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T01:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T01:36:16Z","body":"> I would:\r\n> \r\n> * skip all `elif` cases, since it's not helpful to add last case comment.\r\n> * skip all cases where `if/else` body is 1-3 lines long.\r\n> * add script to pre-commit/CI config (to run on changed files, like `misc/scripts/header_guards.py` and other checks).\r\n\r\nAdded the requested changes. I'm not 100% certain if the naming of it is good or not (I struggle with naming files/functions/kids/folders/stuff...).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5419391545/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434359397","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5434359397","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5434359397,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ-m-ZQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T04:24:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T04:24:36Z","body":"This is way too much code churn for so little benefit. It's fine to add more comments as you change files. But touching 600 files at once and potentially creating merge conflicts with tons of PRs for such little benefit is not worth it IMO","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434359397/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":4,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":4,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434515140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5434515140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5434515140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ-wexA","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T04:49:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T04:49:09Z","body":"> This is way too much code churn for so little benefit. It's fine to add more comments as you change files. But touching 600 files at once and potentially creating merge conflicts with tons of PRs for such little benefit is not worth it IMO\r\n\r\nI agree that it might give merge conflicts of existing PR's, but the headaches of not having those comments in those places is just as (if not more) frustrating for people creating PR's imo. The only parts where merge conflicts happen is with the PR's who touched those ifdef's directly, for the others it's just a rebase on master.\r\n\r\nClean code is important, not having the same \"style\" everywhere is annoying. Having this automated helps towards cleaner and more readable code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434515140/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434921270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5434921270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5434921270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ_JRNg","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T05:48:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T05:48:06Z","body":"I agree with Clay that it's a lot of code churn, and IMO it's not actually making code more readable.\r\n\r\nI think it's useful to put some comments on `#endif` when there are nested conditions, or the branch spans many lines of code (like more than 10 lines at least).\r\n\r\nBut there are a lot of cases where the changes are IMO worse than not having comments:\r\n- Complex conditions that are to parse as a comment\r\n- `#else` branches\r\n- `#endif` after an `#else` or #elseif` branch\r\n- `#endif` ending a negative conditional with `#ifndef` or `#if !`.\r\n\r\nI used to be in favor of more consistently use such comments, and I've added a lot manually, and found the reasons above which convinced me over time that it's not actually a good idea.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434921270/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434935361","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5434935361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5434935361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ_KIQQ","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T05:50:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T05:50:01Z","body":"While I'm also a fan of marking end of `define` blocks (and `for` blocks occasionally) , imo it only helps for clarity **in a subset of these cases** (especially nested), and in the other cases it can actually add _extra_ mental load in reading the code / verbosity.\r\n\r\nI'm pretty sure I've added such comments in my previous PRs _where they help readability_.\r\n\r\n> Clean code is important, not having the same \"style\" everywhere is annoying.\r\n\r\nThe project has to deal with the problem of PRs repeatedly adjusting the same style issues back and forth depending on the preferences of the particular contributor. That's why we have style guides, and outside of that there's a fair amount of leeway.\r\n\r\nSo in general I'm in agreement with @clayjohn here, and probably just adjusting where required when making a PR on a particular section of code is more appropriate.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434935361/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5435388874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797#issuecomment-5435388874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","id":5435388874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ_lzyg","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T06:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T06:47:42Z","body":"Well, good to close then. Thanks for the feedback anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5435388874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]